    {
      "id": "M025",
      "text": "For flaky cache races: reproduce under -race, add synchronization at the ownership boundary, then rerun the focused race test before the whole package.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-02T10:00:00+00:00",
      "session_id": "s12",
      "scope": "repo:demo",
      "metadata": {
        "procedure_family": "race"
      },
      "supersedes_id": null,
      "outcome": "success"
    },
    {
      "id": "M026",
      "text": "Adding sleeps around the cache race reduced failures locally but hidden stress tests still failed; do not use timing sleeps as the fix.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-02T10:20:00+00:00",
      "session_id": "s12",
      "scope": "repo:demo",
      "metadata": {
        "procedure_family": "race"
      },
      "supersedes_id": null,
      "outcome": "failure"
    },
    {
      "id": "M027",
      "text": "For NDJSON protocol bugs: capture exact frames, validate one JSON object per line, and keep logs off stdout; this resolved the bridge desynchronization.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-03T10:00:00+00:00",
      "session_id": "s13",
      "scope": "repo:demo",
      "metadata": {
        "procedure_family": "ndjson"
      },
      "supersedes_id": null,
      "outcome": "success"
    },
    {
      "id": "M028",
      "text": "Pretty-printing outbound JSON across multiple lines made bridge framing failures worse and was reverted.",
      "timestamp": "2026-04-03T10:20:00+00:00",
      "session_id": "s13",
      "scope": "repo:demo",
      "metadata": {
        "procedure_family": "ndjson"
      },
      "supersedes_id": null,
      "outcome": "failure"
